   "text": "1. The image followed the credibility of American commitments",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "Why these documents: they are the officials' own statements of what Asian opinion of the United States turned on, from Jessup's 1949 outline to the post-Indochina post reports and the Carter administration's public diplomacy. The thread is the belief that policy and staying power, not culture, set the image."
